# A change to any file that DEFINES or EXECUTES what a required check
# actually enforces requires a review from a code owner, never satisfiable
# by the PR author's own approval of their own PR. This is the
# tamper-evidence measure for every required check: each one's real content
# lives in files under repo control, so an edit that silently weakens one
# (making check-resolved.sh always exit 0; dropping a hook entry from
# .pre-commit-config.yaml so the "pre-commit" check still reports green with
# less actually checked; blanking .yamllint.yaml or disabling NoEmDash in
# styles/House/ so yamllint/vale silently stop catching anything while
# "pre-commit" still reports green; redefining mise.toml's test task to a
# no-op; weakening validate-commit-msg.sh so commitlint stops catching
# anything; swallowing a failure inside scripts/mise/test.sh so shell-tests
# reports green regardless of what scripts/tests/*.bash actually assert;
# editing configure-protection.sh to drop a check from the required list, or
# flip require_code_owner_reviews back to false; flipping
# .harnx/instance-config.toml's identity_policy from "private" to "public", or
# widening its allowed_authors, so a commit author the repo previously refused
# is silently accepted) must itself pass human review before it can merge.
# This list is systematically derived from
# .pre-commit-config.yaml's own hook entries and their referenced config
# files, not built up finding by finding: every hook that gates the
# required "pre-commit" check, plus every file that gates the other eight
# required checks (gitleaks, actionlint, shell-tests, commitlint,
# branch-name, pr-title, pr-body, ai-review-resolved), is covered below.
/scripts/ai-review/ @fabioluiz1
/scripts/git-discipline/ @fabioluiz1
/scripts/tests/ @fabioluiz1
/scripts/mise/ @fabioluiz1
/scripts/configure-protection.sh @fabioluiz1
/.github/workflows/ @fabioluiz1
/.github/CODEOWNERS @fabioluiz1
# AGENTS.md is here for a different reason than everything else on this list,
# and the distinction is worth keeping straight. Every other entry DEFINES or
# EXECUTES a required check, so editing it can make a gate pass that should
# have failed. AGENTS.md executes nothing and gates nothing: no check reads it,
# and editing it cannot turn a red check green.
#
# It is protected because this repository is an agentic-development harness and
# AGENTS.md is the instruction set agents read before acting. A silent edit
# cannot weaken a gate, but it can change what an agent believes it is supposed
# to do, which is a distinct kind of tampering that the rest of this list does
# not cover.
/AGENTS.md @fabioluiz1
/.pre-commit-config.yaml @fabioluiz1
/.harnx/instance-config.toml @fabioluiz1
/mise.toml @fabioluiz1
/.yamllint.yaml @fabioluiz1
